// =============================================================
// Topic Control Rail — Input
// =============================================================
// Blocks questions that are not about company policy documents.
// DocMind is a policy Q&A assistant, not a general chatbot.
//
// If the user asks about weather, coding, general knowledge, etc.
// this rail intercepts and returns a refusal before any retrieval
// or LLM generation happens — saving API cost and staying on-domain.
// =============================================================

define user ask about policy
  "How many casual leaves do I get?"
  "What is the notice period?"
  "Can I carry forward my sick leaves?"
  "What are the standard working hours?"
  "How much is the health insurance coverage?"
  "What is the overtime pay rate?"
  "Tell me about the leave policy"
  "What is the PF contribution percentage?"
  "Can I work remotely?"
  "What happens if I'm late to work?"

define user ask off topic
  "What's the weather today?"
  "Write me a Python script"
  "Tell me a joke"
  "Who won the last election?"
  "What is the capital of France?"
  "How do I cook pasta?"
  "Can you help me with my math homework?"
  "Write a poem about the ocean"
  "What movies are playing this weekend?"
  "Tell me about the latest news"

define bot refuse off topic
  "I'm a company policy assistant. I can only answer questions about your organization's policies — leave, attendance, compensation, conduct, and separation. Please ask a policy-related question."

define flow topic control
  user ask off topic
  bot refuse off topic
